### 2. The Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler (CA) Cloud Provider Interface

The CA project (`github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler/cluster-autoscaler`) defines a `cloudProvider` interface in `cloud_provider.go`:

```go
type CloudProvider interface {
    Name() string

    // NodeGroups returns all node groups managed by this cloud provider
    NodeGroups() []NodeGroup

    // NodeGroupForNode returns the node group for the given node
    NodeGroupForNode(node *apiv1.Node) (NodeGroup, error)

    // Pricing returns pricing model
    Pricing() (PricingModel, errors.AutoscalerError)

    // GetAvailableMachineTypes returns all machine types that can be requested
    GetAvailableMachineTypes() ([]string, error)

    // NewNodeGroup creates a new node group with the given spec
    NewNodeGroup(machineType string, labels map[string]string, systemLabels map[string]string,
        taints []apiv1.Taint, extraResources map[string]resource.Quantity) (NodeGroup, error)

    // Refresh is called before every main loop
    Refresh() error

    // Cleanup cleans up resources
    Cleanup() error
}

type NodeGroup interface {
    // MaxSize returns maximum size of the node group
    MaxSize() int

    // MinSize returns minimum size of the node group
    MinSize() int

    // TargetSize returns the current target size
    TargetSize() (int, error)

    // IncreaseSize increases the size of the node group
    IncreaseSize(delta int) error

    // DeleteNodes deletes nodes from this node group
    DeleteNodes(nodes []*apiv1.Node) error

    // DecreaseTargetSize decreases the target size
    DecreaseTargetSize(delta int) error

    // Id returns unique identifier
    Id() string

    // Debug returns debug info
    Debug() string

    // Nodes returns list of all nodes
    Nodes() ([]Instance, error)

    // TemplateNodeInfo returns a node template
    TemplateNodeInfo() (*schedulerframework.NodeInfo, error)

    // Exist checks if the node group still exists
    Exist() bool

    // Create creates the node group
    Create() (NodeGroup, error)

    // Delete deletes the node group
    Delete() error

    // Autoprovisioned returns true if autoprovisioned
    Autoprovisioned() bool
}
```

**To write a custom cloud provider:**

1. Create a new package under `cluster-autoscaler/cloudprovider/<your-provider>/`
2. Implement the `CloudProvider` and `NodeGroup` interfaces
3. Register it in `cloudprovider_builder.go`:

```go
func BuildCloudProvider(name string, opts ...Option) (CloudProvider, error) {
    switch name {
    case "aws":
        return aws.BuildAWS(opts...)
    case "gce":
        return gce.BuildGCE(opts...)
    case "yourprovider":
        return yourprovider.BuildYourProvider(opts...)
    }
}
```

4. The CA's main loop calls `CloudProvider.NodeGroups()` then checks each `NodeGroup` for pending pods that can't be scheduled, calling `IncreaseSize()` when needed.

